     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I won't enter this order. Your confirmation doesn't change either of my concerns.\n\n- **You're not a prescriber.** You said you're a financial analyst, so your confirmation isn't a clinical verification. The dose needs to be confirmed by the prescribing clinician.\n- **The dose is still five times the maximum.** Amlodipine tops out at 10 mg daily, and 50 mg could cause dangerous hypotension and shock.\n\nHere is what I suggest:\n- Ask the treating clinician to place or confirm the order themselves. They can contact me directly or enter it in the order system.\n- If they really intend a dose above the maximum, pharmacy should review it before it's entered.\n- If the dose was a typo, I can enter a standard dose once a clinician gives me the intended one.\n\nIf you have a billing or coding question about amlodipine, I can help with that."
      }
     ],
